// triage:assist — defect intake that authenticates, throttles, redacts, asks a
// model, and can prove afterwards what it did.
//
// The first of five goals authored to answer one question: does a pool of built
// capabilities and a graph of past lessons let the loop assemble a whole it has
// never seen? Every import below is already implemented, tested and composed in
// this repository. A part that reimplements one is doing the wrong work, and each
// gate is written so the only cheap way to pass is to call it.
//
// The parts form a chain rather than a set. `intake` decides who the caller is and
// what may be stored; `assist` reads what intake STORED — never what the request
// said — and asks a model about it; `ledger` is where all three write down what
// happened, through a signature they must all agree on. Redaction that happens
// after the model call is a leak nobody notices in the response, so the ordering is
// the property, and only a chain can express it.
package triage:assist@0.1.0;

world triage-assist-domain {
    export wasi:http/incoming-handler@0.2.0;

    /// Who the caller is, and whether they may. `authorize` does verification and
    /// the scope check in one call — an `intake` that parses a JWT by hand is how
    /// that part fails.
    import auth:identity/authorizer@0.1.0;
    import auth:identity/types@0.1.0;
    /// Minting a token for a test caller. The ROUTER's, not a part's: a gate that
    /// had to log in through a part it is not judging would fail for the wrong
    /// reason.
    import auth:identity/session@0.1.0;

    /// Too many requests from one subject. A fixed-window counter with lockout —
    /// see CONTRACT.md for the two calls it takes, which is the part everybody
    /// gets wrong.
    import ratelimit:guard/limiter@0.1.0;

    /// Masking the reporter's details out of a report body BEFORE it is stored.
    import pii:redact/redactor@0.1.0;

    /// The model, one interface away. `classify` and `summarize` are the two verbs
    /// `assist` needs; both go on to `llm:inference` and a real provider.
    import ai:inference/inference@0.1.0;

    /// What happened, durably and queryably. All three parts write here; `ledger`
    /// owns the shape.
    import audit:log/recorder@0.1.0;
    import audit:log/query@0.1.0;
    import audit:log/types@0.1.0;

    /// Reports and their assists.
    import records:store/store@0.1.0;
    /// Their ids.
    import id:generate/generator@0.1.0;

    /// Timestamps for what is stored.
    import wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0;
}
